{"claims":[{"claim_text":"Sequestration, which is severe, automatic, across-the-board cuts in defense spending over the next decade, would be a disaster for national security, imperiling the safety of servicemen and women, accelerating the decline of the nation's defense industrial base, and resulting in the layoff of more than 1 million skilled workers.", "claim_types":["evaluation", "prediction"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Opposition to sequester is bipartisan.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The current Secretary of Defense has said the cuts will be \"devastating\" to America's military.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The current President supported sequestration, signed it into law, and has threatened to veto Republican efforts to prevent it.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"If the current President allows an additional half trillion dollars to be cut from the defense budget, America will be left with the smallest ground force since 1940.", "claim_types":["prediction"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"If the current President allows an additional half trillion dollars to be cut from the defense budget, America will be left with the smallest number of ships since 1915.", "claim_types":["prediction"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"If the current President allows an additional half trillion dollars to be cut from the defense budget, America will be left with the smallest Air Force in its history.", "claim_types":["prediction"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"America faces a growing range of threats to its national security.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"America's economy can ill afford to lose 1.5 million defense-related jobs.", "claim_types":["evaluation"],"evidence_ids":[1]}],"unresolved_references":[]}
```

